{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZZwfAeY6QwZ4JmwhVHs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my exploration, I now have a complete picture of the existing codebase. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that atomically transitions an `ACTIVE` order to `CANCELLED`, cancels its `CREATED` shipments, allows idempotent retries on already-cancelled orders, rejects with 409 (no changes) if any shipment is `CONFIRMED`, rejects with 404 for non-existent orders, and prevents shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt:11-16` — Order entity lacks status field\n- `OrderController.kt:21-46` — Uses exception-based error handling pattern\n- `OrderRepository.kt:11-27` — In-memory ConcurrentHashMap store\n- `Shipment.kt:9-27` — Already has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` — Lacks method to find shipments by orderId\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:11-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-29` — Centralizes error response formatting\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Exception-based error handling with ApiException hierarchy\n2. Endpoints return proper HTTP status codes (201 for created, 404/409 for errors)\n3. In-memory repositories using ConcurrentHashMap\n4. Test pattern: @SpringBootTest with MockMvc assertions on both status and error envelope\n5. Error responses use centralized GlobalExceptionHandler\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — Add `status: OrderStatus` field; needed for lifecycle tracking\n2. `OrderController.kt` — Add POST `/orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint; core requirement\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Add `findByOrderId()` method; needed to find and cancel shipments\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add check to reject shipment creation on cancelled orders; required by spec\n5. `ApiError.kt` — Add error codes for cancel-specific failures; needed for informative errors\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Add cancel endpoint tests; verify all cases\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add test for shipment creation on cancelled order; verify rejection\n\n**Risks:**\n- Race conditions if two cancel requests arrive concurrently (both check, both proceed) → need atomic check-and-update\n- Adding status field to Order requires all Order creations to specify it (backward compatibility within code)\n- Shipment cancellation must be transactional with order cancellation\n\n**Open questions:** None; requirement is complete.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` enum and include `status` field in Order data class. New orders default to `ACTIVE`.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 (ResourceNotFoundException) if order doesn't exist\n   - Returns 200 with cancelled order if already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Returns 409 (ConflictException) if any shipment is CONFIRMED (with no changes)\n   - Otherwise: cancels order, cancels all CREATED shipments, returns 200 with cancelled order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to query shipments by order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Modify POST `/shipments` create endpoint to check if the order's status is CANCELLED and reject with 409 (ConflictException).\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Add ErrorCode values: `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` (for cancel rejection), `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for shipment rejection).\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests:\n   - Cancel active order with no shipments → returns 200 with cancelled order\n   - Cancel active order with CREATED shipments → cancels them, returns 200\n   - Cancel already-cancelled order → returns 200, no changes\n   - Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment → returns 409, order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED\n   - Cancel non-existent order → returns 404\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test:\n   - Create shipment for cancelled order → returns 409\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using a separate service class for cancel logic: The codebase is simple enough that adding the logic directly to the controller (following existing pattern for create) is appropriate. A separate service would add unnecessary abstraction for this scope.\n- Using optimistic locking instead of synchronization: The in-memory store with ConcurrentHashMap is already thread-safe at the Map level. Checking for CONFIRMED shipments and then updating is atomic within a single method.\n- Adding new endpoint like PUT instead of POST: The requirement specifically asks for POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel, which is the RPC-style pattern already used (like POST /shipments).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Check | Action | Write | Response |\n|------|-------|------|-------|--------|-------|----------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE, no shipments | orderId | Order (ACTIVE) | — | Set Order.status = CANCELLED | Order | 200 Order |\n| Cancel ACTIVE with CREATED ships | orderId | Order, Shipments | — | Set Order.status = CANCELLED; Set each ship.status = CANCELLED | Order, Shipments | 200 Order |\n| Cancel ACTIVE with CONFIRMED ship | orderId | Order, Shipments | Any ship.status == CONFIRMED | Abort | — | 409 ConflictException ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT |\n| Cancel CANCELLED (retry) | orderId | Order (CANCELLED) | — | None | — | 200 Order |\n| Cancel non-existent | orderId | Order | Not found | — | — | 404 ResourceNotFoundException ORDER_NOT_FOUND |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED | orderId, shipmentId | Order (CANCELLED), Shipment | Order.status == CANCELLED | Abort | — | 409 ConflictException ORDER_CANCELLED |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. **ActiveOrderNoCancelled** — Create order, call cancel → order is CANCELLED, returns 200\n2. **CancelActiveOrderWithCreatedShipments** — Create order, create 2 CREATED shipments, call cancel → order CANCELLED, both shipments CANCELLED, returns 200\n3. **CancelIdempotent** — Create order, cancel twice → second cancel returns 200, no changes\n4. **CancelWithConfirmedShipmentReturns409** — Create order, create CONFIRMED shipment (write directly to repo), call cancel → returns 409, order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED\n5. **CancelNonExistentOrderReturns404** — Call cancel on non-existent ID → returns 404\n6. **ShipmentCreationRejectsCancelledOrder** — Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment → returns 409\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2306,"cache_read_input_tokens":19530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2306},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6df44517-fc50-4ffd-9712-22e1ac62c4d1","uuid":"d0ebece4-3671-423a-a7ec-08a0b004f567","timestamp":"2026-09-30T11:46:54.006Z","request_id":"req_011CfZZwenqM5eSQVcKGSQHK"}
