 check in create() to reject shipments for cancelled orders. Necessary: required by spec.\n- **ApiError.kt** — Added `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` and `ORDER_CANCELLED` error codes. Necessary: provides informative error responses.\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added shipmentRepository setup and 5 new tests covering all cancel cases. Necessary: verification of implementation.\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added orderRepository setup and 1 new test for cancelled order rejection. Necessary: verification of shipment restriction.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements implemented and tested.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that transitions ACTIVE orders to CANCELLED, cancels CREATED shipments, allows idempotent retries, rejects 409 when CONFIRMED shipments exist, rejects 404 for missing orders, and prevents shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt — Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order (default ACTIVE)\n              OrderController.kt — Added cancel endpoint with atomicity checks and shipment cancellation logic\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — Added findByOrderId() to support cancel operation\n              ShipmentController.kt — Added orderRepository dependency and cancelled order check\n              ApiError.kt — Added ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — Added 5 cancel endpoint tests (basic, with shipments, idempotent, conflict, 404)\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Added 1 test for shipment rejection on cancelled order\n\nTests         1. cancels an active order and returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n              2. cancels an active order and cancels its CREATED shipments atomically\n              3. cancelling an already cancelled order is idempotent (second call succeeds)\n              4. returns 409 with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT when order has CONFIRMED shipment (no changes)\n              5. returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND for non-existent order\n              6. returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED when creating shipment for cancelled order\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, Tests run: 19, Failures: 0, Errors: 0\n              All existing tests (4 order + 5 shipment + 1 app + 3 customer) plus 6 new tests pass\n\nNot done      Nothing — all acceptance criteria addressed, all tests pass, build succeeds\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629,"cache_read_input_tokens":38237,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":629},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6df44517-fc50-4ffd-9712-22e1ac62c4d1","uuid":"093a6603-80fd-451e-9ead-54daf4d55e49","timestamp":"2026-09-30T11:48:41.202Z","request_id":"req_011CfZa6M11J694mg6WnFdBh"}
